Native distributions include Google's shaderc, licensed under Apache-2.0.
See LICENSE.shaderc.apache-2.0 and https://github.com/google/shaderc.

The native libraries are linux/libshaderc_shared.so.1 (Linux), and
windows/shaderc_shared.dll with its import library windows/shaderc_shared.lib
(Windows), built from shaderc by CI.

The shared library also includes glslang, SPIRV-Tools, and SPIRV-Headers.
Their license texts are included under licenses/ in each artifact,
along with shaderc's source revision and upstream dependency pins.
Keep these notices with redistributed binaries.

The C3 binding (shaderc.c3i) is MIT-licensed; see LICENSE.
